# "Custom" Internal Configuration parameters - set by Hobart Only
#
# Config params in this file override the settings in config.dat.
# They can also be specified here, but not exist in config.dat (although that is not the norm!)
#
# The purpose of this file is to have a "custom" setting for one or more internal configuration parameters,
# for a specified customer.  These parameters are controlled by Hobart only.
# This file is not overwritten during the upgrade process, where config.dat is;
# thus, these "customer-specific overrides" will not be lost after upgrading to a
# more recent application version made available to any customer.
#
# Format of commands is 'parameterName=parameterValue'
#
# Comments begin with '#'.  Everything after the comment indicators is ignored.
# Comments can be on their own line, or on the same line as a command.
#
